1. Intent
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The source code in this repository is published for transparency, security
review, feedback, and personal learning. It is NOT published as free software
for others to repackage, rebrand, sell, or operate as a competing product.
Early-stage maintenance and all code changes remain under the copyright
holders' direction.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. What you MAY do (without a separate written license)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

a. View, read, and clone this repository for personal, non-commercial study.
b. Build and run the software locally for personal evaluation and security audit.
c. Quote short excerpts in security research, academic citation, or news
   coverage with clear attribution to the Obscur project and a link to this
   repository.
d. Offer suggestions, bug reports, and review comments through the project's
   public channels (for example Issues). Unsolicited pull requests are not
   requested; the copyright holders alone decide whether and how to change the
   codebase. If you nevertheless submit a patch and it is used, you grant the
   copyright holders a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free license to use,
   modify, and redistribute that material as part of Obscur.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. What you may NOT do (without prior written permission)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

a. Redistribute this software (source or binaries), in whole or in part,
   including mirrors that present it as your product.
b. Repackage, rebrand, fork-and-publish, or wrap this software (or a
   substantial portion of it) as another messenger, client, SaaS, installer,
   or paid/free download.
c. Sell, license, or commercialize this software or derivative works.
d. Remove or obscure copyright, license, or attribution notices.
e. Use this repository's contents to train, fine-tune, or evaluate machine
   learning / AI systems intended for redistribution or commercial use
   (including dataset assembly for that purpose), except as required by
   applicable law or with prior written permission.
f. Use trademarks, logos, or product names of Obscur in a way that suggests
   endorsement or that your product is an official Obscur release.

